opensim-tools: the web side of a grid
=====================================

The scripts the viewers and the simulators query for the economy, the search and the offline messages are the
helpers of this project, in the opensim-helpers package (a dependency of the tools): they are in
/usr/share/opensim-helpers, to be served by a web server. Nothing is enabled by installing the packages. Any other
implementation (w4os, the fork of Kevin Cozens, wiredux) follows the same protocols and can be used instead, nothing
here is needed for it.

Settings
--------

The helpers read the config of the grid: the Robust config of the grid and its helpers.ini, in
/etc/opensim/grids/<grid>/, written by `opensim setup`. Nothing to edit in the helpers. They are specific to a grid:
with several grids on a machine, the virtual host of each one sets OPENSIM_GRID (the snippets below do).

In helpers.ini, the operator chooses:

  [Helpers] path     where the helpers are on the web site (default /helpers, e.g. /helper)
  [Urls]             the public path of a service, when it is not <path>/<script>.php
                     (search = "/search", guide = "/guide", ...)
  [search_db] ...    another database for a service (hostname, prefix, user, password)

Web server
----------

`opensim web` tells where the services are and what answers;
`opensim setup` writes it for the grid in /etc/opensim/grids/<grid>/web (<grid>.caddyfile, <grid>-nginx.conf, <grid>-apache.conf),
`opensim web <grid> snippet caddy|nginx|apache` writes it again, what the web server needs, the aliases of the paths of
helpers.ini included. Include the result in the site of the grid; the config of the web server is not
touched.

helpers.ini holds the password of the database: it is readable by the web server only (group www-data
when the machine has one).
